sxml serialize - Parse an XML document and write it out again

Usage: sxml serialize [--indent] [--method=METHOD] [--output=FILE] [--force] FILE

Parses FILE and writes the document to standard output with the
Serialization 4.0 method that --method names (xml by default) and the
method's default parameters. --indent indents the output.

--output=FILE (-o FILE) writes the document to FILE instead, and only
when FILE (the input) is well-formed; a FILE that exists is replaced
only with --force, which may name the input itself.

A FILE that is not well-formed is reported on standard error as
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: message

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 when FILE is not well-formed or cannot be
serialized, 3 when a file cannot be read or written.

Options:
  -h, --help           Show this help and exit
      --indent         Indent the output
      --method=METHOD  Serialization method (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json, csv; default: xml)
  -o, --output=FILE    Write the result to FILE instead of standard output
      --force          Replace files that exist instead of refusing

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to write; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml serialize --indent draft.xml
  sxml serialize --method=json draft.xml
  sxml serialize --indent --force --output=draft.xml draft.xml
